course: dictionary
lesson: 5920
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Marquis is a noble title from history, but it can also be a first name.
explain: «The friend whispers, "Your dad's wild." Marquis just laughs; he's used to it and kinda likes the order.» Marquis is a person who laughs and gets used to things, so here it is a name. Capital letters and actions like laughing are clues that you are reading about a person.
explain: «In Atlanta, Marquis gets a car for his 17th birthday; Ezekiel got a cheap bike for his 10th.» Marquis and Ezekiel are both people getting presents, so again Marquis is a name. In a history lesson, though, a marquis is a nobleman with a high title.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A marquis is a nobleman with a high title, ranking below a duke and above an earl or count.
fact: In Britain the title is usually spelled «marquess»; France and other countries use «marquis».
fact: The wife of a marquis is a marchioness in Britain, or a marquise in France.
fact: The ladder of titles goes: duke, marquess, earl, viscount, baron.
exercise: In «Marquis just laughs; he's used to it», is Marquis a name or a title? | A castle in France | *A name for a person in the story | A nobleman with a high title | A kind of drink
exercise: What is a marquis? | *A nobleman with a high title, ranking below a duke and above an earl | A king's own son | A French word for a horse | A servant who cooks in a castle
exercise: In Britain, how is the title usually spelled? | *marquess | marquis | marquise | marchioness
test: What is the wife of a marquis called in Britain? | Marquise | Countess | *Marchioness | Duchess
test: Which title comes just below a marquess on the ladder? | *Earl | Baron | Duke | Viscount
exam: In «In Atlanta, Marquis gets a car for his 17th birthday», what is Marquis? | A type of car | A French castle | *A boy's name | A nobleman
